Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 18:33:31 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] images: Option to keep the image's EGL libraries

The host's /vendor/lib{,64}/egl is always bound over the image's. On a
Halium phone those are the vendor's GPU libraries, which the container
cannot use without the vendor's graphics HALs; they hide the image's own
EGL (SwiftShader, Mesa) and SurfaceFlinger aborts with "couldn't find an
OpenGL ES implementation". bind_host_egl = False in [waydroid] keeps the
image's libraries; the default stays as it was.
---
 tools/helpers/images.py | 12 ++++++++----
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/tools/helpers/images.py b/tools/helpers/images.py
index 36bd09b..55ce959 100644
--- a/tools/helpers/images.py
+++ b/tools/helpers/images.py
@@ -184,10 +184,14 @@ def mount_rootfs(args, images_dir, session):
                                     upper_dir=tools.config.defaults["overlay_rw"] + "/vendor",
                                     work_dir=tools.config.defaults["overlay_work"] + "/vendor")
 
-    for egl_path in ["/vendor/lib/egl", "/vendor/lib64/egl"]:
-        if os.path.isdir(egl_path):
-            helpers.mount.bind(
-                args, egl_path, tools.config.defaults["rootfs"] + egl_path)
+    # The host's EGL libraries over the image's: for the host's GPU. bind_host_egl = False in
+    # [waydroid] keeps the image's own (software rendering, or a GPU the host's libraries don't
+    # serve to the container)
+    if cfg["waydroid"].get("bind_host_egl", "True") == "True":
+        for egl_path in ["/vendor/lib/egl", "/vendor/lib64/egl"]:
+            if os.path.isdir(egl_path):
+                helpers.mount.bind(
+                    args, egl_path, tools.config.defaults["rootfs"] + egl_path)
     if helpers.mount.ismount("/odm"):
         helpers.mount.bind(
             args, "/odm", tools.config.defaults["rootfs"] + "/odm_extra")
